<html>
  <head>
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=Cp1252">
    <meta name="generator" content="Helen">
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="../../../../javahelp.css">
    <title>Modifying node properties</title>
  </head>
  <body bgcolor="#ffffff">
    <h1>
       <img border="0" hspace="0" s7starttagpos="281" height="32" width="32" src=
      "../../../../images/carmenHelpIcons/c3_32.gif">&nbsp;&nbsp; Modifying node properties
    </h1>
    <table border="1" cellpadding="4" cellspacing="0" bordercolor="#000000" width="489">
      <col width="234">
      <col width="237">
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="479">
          <p class="western" align="left">
             <b><font size="2">Use case: Modifying node properties</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="479">
          <p class="western" align="left">
             <b><font size="2">Comment:</font></b> <font size="2">To edit the properties of a node,
            it is necessary that only one node and nothing else is been selected, by following the
            steps listed in the table.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="479">
          <p class="western" align="left">
             <b><font size="2">Actor: User</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p class="western" align="left">
             <b><font size="2">Normal course</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p class="western" align="left">
             <b><font size="2">Alternative courses</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">1.The user selects just one node and not any link using any of these
            use cases explained above.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" class=
          "western" align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">2.When the type of editing is the selection of objects, the user double
            presses on a node or presses the option to edit the properties of a node which is in
            the main menu or in the pop-up menu.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" class=
          "western" align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">3.A dialog box appears where the properties of the node can be modified
            excepting its name, its type and the type of its variable.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" class=
          "western" align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">4.The user changes the properties by writing or selecting new
            values.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">4.1.The user can cancel the operation so the use case will end.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">5.The user can add or remove nodes from the table of the parent nodes
            of the node which is being edited. In this table will not may appear neither the node
            that is being edited either its direct child nodes.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">5.1.The user can cancel the operation so the use case will end.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">6.The user accepts the properties changes.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">6.1.The user can cancel the operation so the use case will end.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">7.The program checks if the data given by the user are correct.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">7.1.If a data is not correct, the program informs the user and goes to
            point 4.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">8.If the name of the node has been changed, it will be showed in the
            network node according to the type of presentation of the nodes (by name or by
            title).</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" class=
          "western" align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">9.All the links between the node modified and the nodes that have been
            deleted from the parents node list are deleted.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" class=
          "western" align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">10.Links between the nodes that were added to the list of parents and
            the node modified are added.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" class=
          "western" align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">11.A new point to undo and redo the modification of the node properties
            is created.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" class=
          "western" align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">12.The use case <i>Updating menus when modifying a network</i> is
            executed.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" class=
          "western" align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">13.The network is marked as modified (if it was not already), placing
            an asterisk at the title of the window in which is being editing.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" class=
          "western" align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">14.If necessary, the network panel is resized to house the entire
            network.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" class=
          "western" align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    <p>
       &nbsp;
    </p>
  </body>
</html>
